    {
      "id": "K2G0XdQhn7yuuXjAJ5V0t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2133.9704853438434,
      "y": 77742.2994418987,
      "width": 418,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 103953071,
      "version": 230,
      "versionNonce": 1324116609,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778898571681,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "if username and password is correct\nit will create a token and send it to\nclient, from next time it will say\njust send me this token.\nand it will verify without hitting db.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "if username and password is correct\nit will create a token and send it to\nclient, from next time it will say\njust send me this token.\nand it will verify without hitting db.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "BBYudI44j-50Ii4Ur-dVk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1626.935044404559,
      "y": 78013.86346236047,
      "width": 682,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1077322241,
      "version": 75,
      "versionNonce": 1013873825,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778898628584,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "How Server make sure this is a valid token without hitting db?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "How Server make sure this is a valid token without hitting db?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YcMixUHWudDaH-JftbUhw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1661.1049544829389,
      "y": 78048.52435173259,
      "width": 1364,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnJ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 996852751,
      "version": 960,
      "versionNonce": 2039966305,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778900039053,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "with the help of jwt\nit has 3 parts, header, payload, signature\n\nit will hash\n\nheader -> base64decoded(contains info like what is the type of token like jwt) {\n  \"alg\": \"HS256\",\n  \"typ\": \"JWT\"\n} anyone can read\n\npayload -> base64decoded( contain info like which user, from howmuch time it is valid), anyone can decode it.\n{\n  \"user_id\": 123,\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n} anyone can read.\n\nsignature -> HMACSHA256(base64decoded(header) + base64decoded(payload) + secret) create a secure signature using that secret\n                                                we can again create same signature using secret. and same sigining algo \n                                                HS256 → HMAC + SHA256\n                                                RS256 → RSA\n                                                HS256 = HMACSHA256\n                                                 HMACSHA256 is one way, from data we can easily generate\n                                                signature but from signature its practically impossible\n                                                to reverse hash back to to its original secret.\n \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "with the help of jwt\nit has 3 parts, header, payload, signature\n\nit will hash\n\nheader -> base64decoded(contains info like what is the type of token like jwt) {\n  \"alg\": \"HS256\",\n  \"typ\": \"JWT\"\n} anyone can read\n\npayload -> base64decoded( contain info like which user, from howmuch time it is valid), anyone can decode it.\n{\n  \"user_id\": 123,\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n} anyone can read.\n\nsignature -> HMACSHA256(base64decoded(header) + base64decoded(payload) + secret) create a secure signature using that secret\n                                                we can again create same signature using secret. and same sigining algo \n                                                HS256 → HMAC + SHA256\n                                                RS256 → RSA\n                                                HS256 = HMACSHA256\n                                                 HMACSHA256 is one way, from data we can easily generate\n                                                signature but from signature its practically impossible\n                                                to reverse hash back to to its original secret.\n \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "apcQH85h9USfBKaseKzAS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1651.9974759822821,
      "y": 78765.51153368043,
      "width": 1067,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 993461793,
      "version": 235,
      "versionNonce": 643925551,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778900175978,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Problem -> if this jwt token has stolen by hacker, then he can also access to our account. due to\n    that these tokens are short lived lets say 30 minute, so hacker can only access till 30minute",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Problem -> if this jwt token has stolen by hacker, then he can also access to our account. due to\n    that these tokens are short lived lets say 30 minute, so hacker can only access till 30minute",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "oph3qzLD9_qBruP1QpYyv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1649.4638729096723,
      "y": 78889.91294371919,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 962731009,
      "version": 859,
      "versionNonce": 2082637039,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778900786655,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "this is also worse our User experience due to in every 30 minute we need to say please login, so \nhere we also give one more token that is known as refresh token and this validity is longeer\nlets say 7 days. and this refresh token is not a jwt, this is simpally a token like session id,\nand this token is also stored in database with validity. and server will give user both, access\ntoken and refresh token. Access token might be stolen by third party. refresh token cant be stolen\neasily.\nrefresh token is used to regenerate access token.\n\nif we know that access token is stolen, then we can use redis for blacklisted token. so everytime we\nwill check our token is not a blacklisted token.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "this is also worse our User experience due to in every 30 minute we need to say please login, so \nhere we also give one more token that is known as refresh token and this validity is longeer\nlets say 7 days. and this refresh token is not a jwt, this is simpally a token like session id,\nand this token is also stored in database with validity. and server will give user both, access\ntoken and refresh token. Access token might be stolen by third party. refresh token cant be stolen\neasily.\nrefresh token is used to regenerate access token.\n\nif we know that access token is stolen, then we can use redis for blacklisted token. so everytime we\nwill check our token is not a blacklisted token.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZUq64Iel_AHgh0J1UHjyx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1570.8547148550567,
      "y": 79255.88779502516,
      "width": 169.39993286132812,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 637982543,
      "version": 60,
      "versionNonce": 34684289,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1778900864375,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SSH keys ->",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SSH keys ->",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
